      "message": "The context is that on many occasions, I\u0027ve wanted to understand the performance impact of a change I made.\n\nThe particular occasion right now that triggered this is that I want to understand the impact of making ninja files per directory instead of per-target. Without tracelogs, it\u0027s a lot harder to get statistically significant / useful data. Because this can analyze the precise impact on a particular part of the build rather than the whole build, it\u0027s a lot easier to see, for example, that a change that adds 30ms which isn\u0027t statistically significant, actually reliably adds 30ms to this specific part of the build, which is statistically significant.",
